   "source": [
    "# Shopify Bookstore - Complete Integration Guide
",
    "
",
    "This notebook teaches you how to build a complete bookstore using Shopify API.
",
    "
",
    "## What You'll Learn:
",
    "- Shopify API authentication
",
    "- Creating and managing book products
",
    "- Inventory management
",
    "- Order processing
",
    "- Customer management
",
    "- Storefront integration
",
    "- Custom React frontend
",
    "
",
    "## Prerequisites:
",
    "- Shopify Partner account (free at https://partners.shopify.com)
",
    "- Development store
",
    "- Node.js installed
",
    "- Basic React knowledge
",
    "
",
    "Run cells one by one from top to bottom.
"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "setup-markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Shopify Setup and API Credentials
",
    "
",
    "First, set up your Shopify development store and get API credentials.
"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "setup-code",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "/*
",
    "SHOPIFY SETUP STEPS:
",
    "
",
    "1. Create Shopify Partner Account:
",
    "   - Go to https://partners.shopify.com
",
    "   - Sign up for free
",
    "   - Create a development store
",
    "
",
    "2. Create Custom App:
",
    "   - In your store admin, go to Settings > Apps and sales channels
",
    "   - Click \"Develop apps\"
",
    "   - Click \"Create an app\"
",
    "   - Name it \"Bookstore API\"
",
    "   - Configure API scopes:
",
    "     * read_products, write_products
",
    "     * read_orders, write_orders
",
    "     * read_customers, write_customers
",
    "     * read_inventory, write_inventory
",
    "   - Install the app
",
    "   - Get Admin API access token
",
    "